# Cloudflare Workers Static Assets (and Cloudflare Pages) both read this
# file from the root of the deployed static asset directory and apply these
# headers to every static-asset response (the SPA shell, its JS/CSS bundles,
# and any other file under apps/web/dist). It has no effect on responses the
# Worker's own fetch() code generates (apps/api/src/index.ts sets its own
# security headers directly -- see the SECURITY_HEADERS constant there).
#
# This dashboard is a private, authenticated-only SPA with no third-party
# embeds, inline scripts, or inline <style> blocks (all styling ships as a
# single linked apps/web/src/styles.css, and Vite emits only external
# module/script/link tags -- see apps/web/index.html) -- so every directive
# below is scoped to 'self' rather than allowing any inline or third-party
# source.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Cache-Control: private, no-store

# Vite content-hashes every file it emits under /assets/* (e.g.
# assets/index-<hash>.js, assets/index-<hash>.css) -- a filename only ever
# refers to one immutable set of bytes, so a stale cached copy is
# impossible: a code change always ships under a new hashed filename. The
# blanket `/*` rule above (still applied for the security headers, matched
# together with this more specific rule per Cloudflare's "most specific
# path wins per header" merge) sets `no-store` for everything, which is
# correct for index.html (must always be revalidated so it picks up the
# latest hashed asset filenames) but needlessly forces a network round trip
# for every hashed bundle on every request. This still keeps caching
# `private` (this is an Access-gated app, never a shared/public cache) --
# only the freshness window changes, from "never cache" to "cache exactly
# as long as the filename is guaranteed to mean the same bytes."
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: private, max-age=31536000, immutable
